## 1. Quick Overview
- What: AWS is a broad cloud platform providing managed services for compute, storage, databases, networking, analytics, ML, security, migration, developer tools and more.
- How to read names: Service names usually indicate purpose (EC2 = compute, S3 = storage, RDS = relational DB). Some services are named after OSS tech they manage (EKS = Kubernetes, OpenSearch = Elast[...]
- Study tip: Group services by function (Compute, Storage, Database, Networking, Security, DevOps, ML) — this reduces memorization work.

