## 2. Compute
**Concept:** Run code or VMs in the cloud: virtual machines, containers, serverless, batch/orchestration, hybrid.

Key services:
- Amazon EC2 — virtual servers (instance types, AMIs, EBS volumes).
- AWS Lambda — serverless functions; billed per invocation and execution time.
- AWS Fargate — serverless containers (runs ECS/EKS tasks/pods).
- AWS Batch — managed batch job orchestration (provisions compute as needed).
- AWS Elastic Beanstalk — PaaS for quick app deployments.
- Amazon Lightsail — simplified VPS with predictable pricing.
- AWS Outposts — AWS-managed hardware & services on-premises for hybrid workloads.

When to use:
- EC2: full OS control, specialized hardware (GPU/HPC), long-running servers.
- Lambda: event-driven or short-lived processes, microservices, APIs.
- Fargate: container workloads without node management.
- Batch: large-scale batch processing.

Exam tips:
- Billing differences (EC2 = instance-hours; Lambda = invocations+duration).
- Understand cold starts and Provisioned Concurrency for Lambda.

![EC2 vs Lambda vs Fargate — quick decision table](images/compute-comparison-table.png)


