## 5. Databases (Purpose-built)
**Concept:** Choose databases by access pattern: relational (ACID), NoSQL, in-memory, time-series, graph, ledger.

Key services:
- Amazon RDS — managed relational databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server).
- Amazon Aurora — MySQL/Postgres-compatible, high-performance cluster.
- Amazon Redshift — data warehouse for OLAP.
- Amazon DynamoDB — fully managed NoSQL key-value/document DB.
- Amazon DocumentDB — MongoDB-compatible document DB.
- Amazon ElastiCache — Redis / Memcached for in-memory caching.
- Specialized: Neptune (graph), Timestream (time-series), QLDB (ledger), Keyspaces (Cassandra-compatible).

When to use:
- RDS/Aurora for transactional relational workloads.
- DynamoDB for high-scale, low-latency key-value access.
- Redshift for analytics and petabyte-scale warehousing.

Exam tips:
- Multi-AZ vs Read Replicas: Multi-AZ = HA failover; Read replicas = read scaling.
- Know typical integration points (DynamoDB Accelerator, DAX; Aurora read replicas).

![Relational vs NoSQL vs In-memory vs Analytics — use cases](images/db-choice-matrix.png)

