## 10. Networking & Content Delivery
**Concept:** Private networks, route traffic, deliver content globally, and connect on-premises systems.

Key services:
- Amazon VPC — subnets, route tables, NAT, IGW, NACLs, security groups.
- Elastic Load Balancing — ALB (L7), NLB (L4), CLB (legacy).
- Amazon Route 53 — DNS and routing policies.
- Amazon CloudFront — CDN for caching content at edge locations.
- AWS Direct Connect & AWS VPN — private and encrypted connectivity to on-premises.
- AWS PrivateLink, Transit Gateway, App Mesh, Cloud Map.

Exam tips:
- ALB for HTTP/HTTPS (path-based routing, host-based routing), NLB for extreme performance and static IPs.
- Understand public vs private subnets and NAT Gateway behavior.

![VPC with public/private subnets + NAT Gateway](images/vpc-basics.png)

