## 12. Identity & Access Management
**Concept:** Manage identities, authentication, and authorization across AWS and external identity providers.

Key services:
- AWS IAM — users, groups, roles, policies (least privilege, role assumption, STS temporary credentials).
- Amazon Cognito — user sign-up/sign-in (user pools) and AWS credential provisioning (identity pools).
- AWS Single Sign-On (IAM Identity Center) — centralized access to multiple AWS accounts and apps.
- AWS Directory Service — managed Microsoft Active Directory.

Exam tips:
- Distinguish Cognito user pools (authentication) vs identity pools (temporary AWS credentials).
- Understand role assumption and STS temporary credentials.

![IAM role trust relationship](images/iam-role-trust.png)

